diff --git a/docs/decisions/2573-hurco-winmax-post.md b/docs/decisions/2573-hurco-winmax-post.md
index f7974ed5ca..f460b9bd76 100644
--- a/docs/decisions/2573-hurco-winmax-post.md
+++ b/docs/decisions/2573-hurco-winmax-post.md
@@ -78,3 +78,30 @@ Cost to change later: low (`assets/posts/hurco-winmax.cps`,
   **Dropped:** Choosing only one side of the merge conflict.
   Simulator evidence remains pending. No new load results or path comparisons
   were supplied for this fix.
+
+- **Decided (tester report, 2026-11-25):** Write no `G43 H` by default. The
+  option `toolLengthOffset` (default off) writes `G43 H<tool>` after each
+  `T M6`. With the option on, a tool number outside 1..200 is refused by name.
+  **Why:** The tester's WinMax simulator stopped at `G43 H562`. Hurco's online
+  help (Tool and Radius Offsets (G40-G49)) says that with no `G43`/`G44` and no
+  `H` word, the control takes the tool length from the Tool Setup screen. It
+  also gives the `H` range as `H00` to `H200`. `G49` keeps the Tool Setup
+  length (same page, offset table), so the safe start line keeps `G49`.
+  **Dropped:** `G43 H<tool>` as the default; writing an `H` word above 200.
+- **Decided:** `retractAlongToolVector` (default off) writes `G00 M140` at the
+  end of each operation. The next X/Y traverse then states its Z first.
+  `shortestRotaryPath` (default off) writes `M126` after the start line and
+  `M127` before `M30`.
+  **Why:** The tester's 2019 WinMax uses `G0 M140` after each operation and
+  `M126` in the preamble. The online help (Program Functions) documents
+  `M140 [L] [P]` (non-modal, no `L` retracts to the machine limits) and
+  `M126`/`M127`. The 2010 manual (704-0116-310, pages 5-13 and 5-19) says that
+  both work only on the VMX42 SR. Thus the default output does not use them.
+  **Dropped:** `M140` or `M126` in the default output; `M31` (rotary encoder
+  reset), which a 3-axis post does not need.
+- **Deferred:** Tool pre-staging (`T110 M6`, then `T104` on its own line). The
+  online help (Program Functions, "M6 Initiates Tool Change") and the 2010
+  manual (page 4-1) confirm that a `T` word without `M06` pre-fetches the tool
+  when that parameter is Yes. When it is No, a `T` word alone changes the tool.
+  The post also cannot know the next tool: `programTools` is sorted by number,
+  not by tool-change order. Follow-up issue #4113 holds this work.

From 3b5c4da6e3d4d5476ac570cb1a7ba3d8483bf27d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:11:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] fix(post): Hurco WinMax posts no arc block for a sub-step
 arc

Main's #3442 law (radius_arcs: major_arcs_use_negative_r_and_degenerate_
arcs_fall_back_to_ijk) now reaches this post through the merge. An inch
arc of r=0.001 mm wrote `G03 X0. Y0. I0. J0.`, which a control reads as
a full circle. onCircular now asks arcFate (PRELUDE) first, as the other
shipped posts do, with arcIncOf(fu) for the incremental I J K.

comment_escape counts 26 shipped text posts (Hurco is the new one).

Refs #2573

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 assets/posts/hurco-winmax.cps       | 6 ++++++
 crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/assets/posts/hurco-winmax.cps b/assets/posts/hurco-winmax.cps
index 46b3809e47..593701700d 100644
--- a/assets/posts/hurco-winmax.cps
+++ b/assets/posts/hurco-winmax.cps
@@ -758,10 +758,16 @@ function emitRadiusArc(p, g, planeNum, sx, sy, sz, ex, ey, ez, cx, cy, cz, ccw,
   return true;
 }
 
+// #3442: a position word as written, for arcFate (origin-relative, like every X/Y/Z word here).
+function arcWord(k, v) { return k + fu(v - (k === "X" ? orgX : (k === "Y" ? orgY : orgZ))); }
+
 function onCircular() {
   var p = properties;
   seatKnown = true;
   startPreamble();
+  // #3442: an arc whose written ends coincide is no arc block (arcFate, PRELUDE).
+  var fate = arcFate(arcWord, arcIncOf(fu));  // #3474: I J K are increments from the start
+  if (fate !== "arc") { if (fate === "linear") onLinear(); return; }
   if (!tiltOk(p)) return;
   if (inCycle) { msg(who() + "circular arc inside canned-cycle group"); return; }
   var ccw = String(p.CircularDirection || "CW").toUpperCase() === "CCW";
diff --git a/crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs b/crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs
index 3834a63b73..97cf308577 100644
--- a/crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs
+++ b/crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs
@@ -319,6 +319,6 @@ fn header_notes_use_each_shipped_dialect_and_keep_the_full_surface_bound() {
         }
         text_posts += 1;
     }
-    assert_eq!(text_posts, 25, "every shipped text post writes both notes");
+    assert_eq!(text_posts, 26, "every shipped text post writes both notes");
     assert_eq!(native_refusals, 1, "the native Agie dispatcher refused the notes");
 }

